{"id":"farm-products","title":"Farm products worth the most worldwide","prompt":"Name the 10 crops and livestock products with the highest production value worldwide (FAO, 2016)","noun":"farm products","category":"Oddball","metric":"Production value (2016)","blitz":true,"source":{"name":"Wikipedia: List of most valuable crops and livestock products","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_most_valuable_crops_and_livestock_products","asOf":"2026-11-06","dataAsOf":"2016"},"answers":[{"rank":1,"name":"Rice","aliases":["Rice, paddy","paddy","white rice","brown rice"],"value":"$332 billion","n":332,"article":"Rice","fact":{"text":"It's the staple food of over half the world, yet only about 8% of it is traded between countries.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rice"}},{"rank":2,"name":"Pork","aliases":["Pig, meat","Pig","pigs","pigmeat","pork meat","hog","hogs","swine","bacon","ham"],"value":"$280 billion","n":280,"article":"Pork","fact":{"text":"Pigs were domesticated around 13,000 BC in Mesopotamia; ham, bacon and sausage began as ways to keep their meat.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pork"}},{"rank":3,"name":"Beef","aliases":["Cattle, meat","Cattle","cow","cows","cow meat","bovine meat","steak","veal","beef meat"],"value":"$269 billion","n":269,"article":"Beef","fact":{"text":"It has the highest greenhouse gas emissions of any farm product; the US, Brazil and China produce the most.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beef"}},{"rank":4,"name":"Cow's milk","aliases":["cows","Cow's milk, whole fresh","milk","cow milk","dairy milk","whole milk"],"value":"$238 billion","n":238,"article":"Milk","fact":{"text":"In 2011 the world's 260 million dairy cows gave around 730 million tonnes of milk.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milk"}},{"rank":5,"name":"Chicken","aliases":["Chicken, meat","chickens","hen","hens","chicken breast"],"value":"$192 billion","n":192,"article":"Chicken as food","fact":{"text":"There were 19 billion chickens on Eart